# mixed-code-defined-as root
library "Mixed".

// A multi-layer library where one concept carries BOTH a local `code is` and a
// `defined as`. The mixed concept is unclassifiable, so the whole library stays
// on the per-CRL path (NOT auto-split) until the code-is slice.

terminology "VS":
- valueset is `vs`.

concept "Leaf":
- type is Observation.
- coded from "VS".

concept "Mixed Concept":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `local-code`.
- defined as "Leaf".
